desktop-shell-tray-click-window-focus(1)

# NAME

desktop-shell-tray-click-window-focus - brings up an application's window when its tray icon is clicked

# SYNOPSIS

*desktop-shell-tray-click-window-focus* [*-c* _FILE_]

# DESCRIPTION

When a tray icon is clicked, sway's bar calls Activate on the icon's
StatusNotifierItem without an activation token, so an application asking
to be shown is only marked urgent. This program watches those calls as a
D-Bus monitor (org.freedesktop.DBus.Monitoring), asks the bus which process
owns the icon, and focuses that process's window through sway's IPC: its
own window, else a parent's or child's. It focuses once at once and once
more shortly after, for applications that open their window on the click.

It reads only Activate calls to tray icons and sends nothing on the bus.
After a package upgrade, *swaymsg reload* restarts it from the new file.

# OPTIONS

*-h, --help*
	Show the help message and exit.

*-c, --config* _FILE_
	Read settings from _FILE_ instead of the usual places.

*-s, --style* _FILE_
	Accepted like by every component; unused.

# SETTINGS

Read from _$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/desktop-shell-components/tray-click-window-focus.ini_,
else _/etc/xdg/desktop-shell-components/tray-click-window-focus.ini_. All are
optional; *swaymsg reload* applies changes.

*[focus]*
	*enabled* = _true_|_false_++
	*second-attempt* = _0-5000_ milliseconds (0 for none)

# SEE ALSO

*sway*(5), *sway-bar*(5), *dbus-monitor*(1)
